---
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Logo from '../../components/Logo.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy | MFD Research';
const description =
  'How MFD Research Group LLC handles information on mfdresearch.com: what we collect, the services that receive it, and your privacy rights, including under California law.';
const canonical = 'https://mfdresearch.com/privacy-policy/';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical}>
  <main class="legal-page wrap">
    <a class="legal-top" href="/" aria-label="MFD Research home">
      <Logo />
    </a>

    <article class="legal-card">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="meta">Last updated: September 28, 2026</p>

      <p>
        This policy explains how MFD Research Group LLC (“MFD Research,” “we,” “us”) collects, uses and protects
        information through this website, <a href="https://mfdresearch.com/">mfdresearch.com</a>, and the inquiries
        you send us through it. Information we receive while providing consulting services to clients is covered by
        our agreements with those clients, not by this policy.
      </p>

      <div class="legal-summary">
        <p><strong>In short</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>We only collect what you choose to send us, such as your name, email and message.</li>
          <li>This website uses no cookies, analytics, advertising or tracking tools.</li>
          <li>We do not sell or share your personal information for advertising.</li>
          <li>Please don't send patient information or confidential study details through this website.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
      <h3>Information you give us</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Contact form:</strong> your first and last name, email address, company (optional), the service
          you're interested in, and your message.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Email:</strong> anything you include when you write to us directly.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Scheduling:</strong> when you book a consultation through our Google Calendar booking page, your
          name, email address and any notes you add.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
      <p>
        Like any website, our hosting provider receives technical information when you visit, such as your IP
        address, browser type, the pages requested and the time of the request. It is used to deliver the site and
        protect it from abuse. We do not use cookies, analytics, advertising pixels or any other tracking technology,
        and our fonts are hosted on our own servers rather than loaded from a third party.
      </p>

      <h3>Information stored on your device</h3>
      <p>
        If you switch between light and dark mode, your browser remembers the choice in its local storage. The site
        also saves a copy of its own files in your browser so pages load faster and work offline. Neither is sent to
        us, and you can clear both at any time in your browser settings.
      </p>

      <h2>Please Don't Send Sensitive Information</h2>
      <p>
        This website is not designed to receive protected health information, patient or study-participant data, or
        confidential or proprietary information about your studies, products or organization. Please don't include it
        in the contact form, a booking or an email. If an engagement requires confidential information, we will agree
        on a confidentiality agreement and a secure way to share it first.
      </p>

      <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To respond to your inquiry and schedule and hold consultations.</li>
        <li>To provide information about our services that you have asked for.</li>
        <li>To keep records of our business communications.</li>
        <li>To keep the website secure and prevent spam and abuse.</li>
        <li>To comply with legal obligations and protect our legal rights.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We won't add you to a marketing list unless you ask us to. We don't use your information for automated
        decision-making or profiling.
      </p>

      <h2>Service Providers</h2>
      <p>We use a small number of service providers, each of which receives only what it needs to do its job:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Web3Forms</strong> receives contact form submissions and delivers them to our inbox
          (<a href="https://web3forms.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google</strong> runs our consultation booking page (Google Calendar). Information you enter there is
          also subject to
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's privacy policy</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts and secures the website
          (<a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>).
        </li>
        <li><strong>Our email provider</strong> stores the messages we send and receive.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Our LinkedIn link takes you to LinkedIn, and nothing is shared with LinkedIn unless you click it. What happens
        on LinkedIn is covered by LinkedIn's own policies.
      </p>

      <h2>When We Share Information</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell personal information, and we do not share it for cross-context behavioral advertising. We
        disclose it only:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>to the service providers listed above, to operate the website and our communications;</li>
        <li>when required by law, or to protect our rights, our clients or others;</li>
        <li>as part of a merger, acquisition or sale of our business, subject to this policy; or</li>
        <li>with your permission.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How Long We Keep It</h2>
      <p>
        We keep inquiry and scheduling information for as long as we need it to respond to you and keep our business
        records, generally no more than three years after our last contact. If you become a client, or the law
        requires us to keep something longer, we keep it for as long as needed for that reason. Hosting logs are
        kept by our hosting provider for a short period under its own policies.
      </p>

      <h2>How We Protect It</h2>
      <p>
        The website is served only over an encrypted connection (HTTPS), and access to inquiries is limited to the
        people who need it to respond. No method of transmission or storage is perfectly secure, which is another
        reason not to send sensitive information through the website.
      </p>

      <h2>Your Privacy Rights</h2>
      <p>Wherever you live, you can ask us to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>tell you what personal information we have about you and give you a copy;</li>
        <li>correct information that is inaccurate; and</li>
        <li>delete your information, unless we need to keep it for a legal reason.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>California residents</h3>
      <p>
        California law, including the California Consumer Privacy Act as amended, gives you the rights above: the
        right to know what personal information we collect, use and disclose; to delete it; and to correct it. It also
        gives you the right to opt out of the sale or sharing of your personal information and to limit the use of
        sensitive personal information. We don't sell or share personal information and don't use sensitive
        personal information, so there is nothing to opt out of or limit. We will not treat you differently for using
        any of these rights. You can use an authorized agent to make a request on your behalf.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not disclose personal information to third parties for their own direct marketing, as described in
        California Civil Code § 1798.83. Because we don't track visitors, we respond to “Do Not Track” and Global
        Privacy Control signals by continuing not to track you.
      </p>

      <h3>Visitors outside the United States</h3>
      <p>
        We are based in the United States, and information you send us is processed there. Where laws such as the
        GDPR apply, we rely on our legitimate interest in responding to inquiries you send us, or on your consent. You
        may also have the right to object to or restrict our use of your information and to complain to your local
        data protection authority.
      </p>

      <h3>Making a request</h3>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:info@mfdresearch.com?subject=Privacy%20request">info@mfdresearch.com</a> with the subject
        “Privacy request.” We may need to confirm your identity, usually by replying to the email address you used to
        contact us. We respond within 45 days, or within one month where the GDPR or UK GDPR applies.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        This website is intended for professionals and is not directed to children under 16. We do not knowingly
        collect information from children. If you believe a child has sent us information, contact us and we will
        delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Other Websites</h2>
      <p>
        Links to other websites, such as LinkedIn, conference sites and our booking page, are governed by those
        sites' own privacy policies.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        If we change this policy, we will post the new version on this page and update the date at the top. If a
        change materially affects information we already hold, we will tell you before it applies to that
        information.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        MFD Research Group LLC<br />
        <a href="mailto:info@mfdresearch.com">info@mfdresearch.com</a>
      </p>
      <p>See also our <a href="/terms-of-service/">Terms of Service</a>.</p>

      <Button href="/" variant="outline" arrow="start" class="home-btn">Back to Home</Button>
    </article>
  </main>

</BaseLayout>
